            "level": 1,
            "value": "So what can we say about helping people to lose weight? There's a lot we could say about what restaurants could do to reduce obesity. I read that the items at the start of a menu and the items at the end of a menu are much more likely to be chosen than the items in the middle. So if you put the low calorie items at the beginning and end of the menu, people will probably go for the food with fewer calories without even realizing what they're doing.",
